      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Foreword",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-000-foreword.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Human health has only ever improved because of advances in technology. From the \ndevelopment of modern sanitation to the advent of penicillin, anesthesia, vaccines and \nmagnetic resonance imaging, science, research and technology have always been key \ndrivers of better health. \nIt’s no different today. Advances in technology are continuing to push back the \nboundaries of disease. Digital technologies enable us to test for diabetes, HIV and malaria \non the spot, instead of sending samples off to a laboratory. 3-D printing is revolutionizing \nthe manufacture of medical devices, orthotics and pro",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The foreword by the WHO Director-General argues that technology has always driven health gains and lists digital advances from point-of-care testing to artificial intelligence. It stresses that countries should be guided by evidence rather than new gadgets and presents this as WHO's first guideline on digital interventions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
