      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Assessment, synthesis and grading of the evidence",
      "pageStart": 47,
      "pageEnd": 50,
      "target": "../sections/sec-017-24-assessment-synthesis-and-grading-of-the-evide.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "of the evidence\nAssessment of risk of bias/methodological limitations of \nprimary studies included in the reviews\nFor the effectiveness studies included in the systematic reviews of the effects of interventions, \nthe risk of bias was assessed using the explicit criteria outlined in the Cochrane handbook for \nsystematic reviews of interventions (45), and the guidance from the Cochrane EPOC group (42). Each \nincluded study was assessed and rated by the review authors as being at low, high or unclear risk \nof bias for each risk-of-bias domain. These assessments provided an overall risk of bias fo",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes how risk of bias in effectiveness studies was assessed using Cochrane methods and how qualitative studies were appraised with an adapted Critical Appraisal Skills Programme tool. It also mentions the WEIRD tool for programme data and the use of GRADE for effectiveness evidence. Confidence in qualitative findings was graded with GRADE-CERQual as high, moderate, low or very low by consensus.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
