      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Implementation components",
      "pageStart": 103,
      "pageEnd": 105,
      "target": "../sections/sec-035-42-implementation-components.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Digital health implementations rely on a host of factors, and their success is often mediated by \nissues intrinsic to the design of the implementation, as well as external factors related to the \nenabling and ICT environment. The implementation of digital health interventions is broadly \npredicated on the following critical components: \ni.\t appropriate and accurate health content and information aligned with recommendation \npractices (e.g. from health programme guidelines or evidence-based normative practices); \nii.\t the digital health intervention, consisting of the discrete digital functiona",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out the components on which digital health implementations depend: accurate health content, the digital intervention itself, the software and communication channels that deliver it, and the ICT and enabling environment. A figure shows how these components combine.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
