      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Overarching implementation considerations",
      "pageStart": 105,
      "pageEnd": 110,
      "target": "../sections/sec-036-43-overarching-implementation-considerations.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Overarching implementation considerations\nImplementations need to be made appropriate to the local needs, intended users, and overall \necosystem comprised of the ICT and enabling environment. The National eHealth strategy \ntoolkit produced jointly by WHO and ITU (18) provides useful considerations for assessing the ICT \nand enabling environment and can be used to help countries in determining their readiness to \nadopt the digital health interventions. \nTable 4.1 \tComponents of the ICT and enabling environment\nComponents of ICT and \nenabling environment\nDescription \nLeadership and \ngovernance\nT",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents overarching considerations for implementing digital health, stressing fit with local needs, users and the ICT and enabling environment, and referring to the WHO–ITU National eHealth Strategy Toolkit for assessing readiness. A table describes components of the enabling environment such as leadership and governance, strategy and investment, legislation, infrastructure and workforce. It closes with principles for digital development, including designing with users, building for scale and sustainability, using open standards, and addressing privacy and security.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
