      "target": "../sections/sec-042-62-updates-and-living-guidelines-approach.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This guideline will be subject to a phased approach that treats them as living guidelines, \nsupporting the review of new evidence for specific questions on digital health interventions. \nThis will ensure that new evidence is brought to the guideline development group (GDG) for \nreview. The first planned update to the guideline will be to include the use of targeted client5 \ncommunication for noncommunicable diseases. A virtual GDG will be convened for formulating \nrecommendations based on the evidence tables prepared for this additional priority question. \nAssociated recommendations will be in",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that the guideline will be treated as a living guideline, with new evidence reviewed as it emerges, and that the first update will add targeted client communication for noncommunicable diseases in version 1.1. It notes the need for continuous scanning of the rapidly changing digital health field.",
